  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0210 database is designed to manage a library's collection of books, authors, members, and librarians. The database contains eight tables: authors, genres, books, members, borrow, librarians, transactions, and book_reviews. The authors table stores information about the library's authors, including their first name, middle name, last name, birth date, nationality, biography, and description. The genres table lists the different genres of books, with each genre having a unique name and description. The books table contains details about each book, such as its title, author ID, genre ID, publication date, ISBN, number of available and total copies, and description. The members table stores information about the library's members, including their first name, middle name, last name, enrollment date, email, phone number, address, and description. The borrow table tracks the borrowing history of each book, with each transaction containing the book ID, member ID, borrowing date, due date, return date, and description. The librarians table stores information about the library's staff, including their first name, middle name, last name, email, phone number, address, and description. The transactions table logs all transactions, including book ID, member ID, librarian ID, transaction date, and transaction type. The book_reviews table contains reviews of books, with each review including the book ID, member ID, rating, comment, review date, and description. The database enforces referential integrity through foreign key constraints, ensuring that a book can only be borrowed by a member who exists in the members table, and that a book can only be reviewed by a member who exists in the members table. Similarly, a librarian can only perform a transaction if they exist in the librarians table. The database also uses primary keys to uniquely identify each record in each table, and indexes are not explicitly defined, but can be automatically created by the database management system to improve query performance.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context  \nThe project involves developing a library management system using the `LibraryCatalog` database. This system is designed to organize and manage information related to books, patrons, loans, and returns in a library environment.\n\n2) Objectives  \nThe primary objective is to facilitate efficient management of library resources, ensuring that books can be easily tracked and managed. This includes handling book inventories, managing patron information, overseeing borrowing and returning processes, and recording transactions.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Stakeholders: Library administrators, head librarians, and IT department.\n- Users: Patrons (members), librarians, and possibly support staff for data entry.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- Books Management: Maintain records of books, including title, author, genre, publication date, and availability.\n- Authors and Genres: Manage and categorize books using author and genre information.\n- Patron Management: Keep detailed records of library members, including personal information and membership details.\n- Loan Management: Track borrowing activities with details such as the borrow date, due date, and return date.\n- Review System: Allow members to review and rate books they have read.\n- Transactions: Log all transactions involving book borrowings, returns, and other library operations with involvement from both members and librarians.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- Performance: The system should handle multiple transactions and queries concurrently without significant delay.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for both members and librarians to perform library operations efficiently.\n- Scalability: Be capable of handling an increasing number of books and members as the library grows.\n- Security: Ensure the protection of member information and transaction data from unauthorized access.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0210.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0210\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `genres` (\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`genre_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`genre_id`) REFERENCES `genres` (`genre_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `members` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `enrollment_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `borrow` (\n  `borrow_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrowing_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `due_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`borrow_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `borrow_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `borrow_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `librarians` (\n  `librarian_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`librarian_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transactions` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `librarian_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`librarian_id`) REFERENCES `librarians` (`librarian_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_reviews` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_reviews_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_reviews_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
